---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'

import '../../styles/ports.css'

import { Badge, ButtonLink, Eyebrow, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import previewDark from '../../../../../packages/santi020k-obsidian-theme/assets/previews/preview-dark.png'
import previewLight from '../../../../../packages/santi020k-obsidian-theme/assets/previews/preview-light.png'
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro'

const description = 'A calm violet Obsidian theme for desktop, iPhone, and iPad, with dark and light notes, readable code, and coordinated navigation.'
---
<ProductLayout name="Obsidian" applicationCategory="ProductivityApplication" slug="obsidian" title="Santi020k Theme for Obsidian — A calmer place for your notes" {description}>
  <section class="site-shell port-hero">
    <div><Eyebrow>Your thoughts, in good company</Eyebrow><h1>Space to think. Room to connect.</h1><p class="lede">Bring the same violet palette to your notes, links, and daily discoveries. Read comfortably in light or dark, at your desk or on your phone.</p><div class="port-meta"><Badge variant="outline">Manual download</Badge><span>Obsidian 1.10.6+</span><span>Dark + light</span></div><div class="port-actions"><ButtonLink class="port-button port-button-primary" variant="unstyled" href="/downloads/ports/santi020k-obsidian.zip" download>Download Obsidian theme</ButtonLink><ButtonLink class="port-button port-button-secondary" href="#install" variant="unstyled">Installation guide</ButtonLink></div></div>
    <figure class="port-figure port-native-preview"><Image class="port-preview-dark" src={previewDark} alt="Obsidian in dark appearance, showing a daily note, violet navigation, code, and a table" widths={[640, 960, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 92vw, 45vw" loading="eager" /><Image class="port-preview-light" src={previewLight} alt="The same Obsidian note in light appearance with a soft violet sidebar" widths={[640, 960, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 92vw, 45vw" loading="eager" /><figcaption>Captured in Obsidian 1.14.4 on macOS · example notes</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section id="install" class="site-shell port-section"><Eyebrow>Start with your vault</Eyebrow><h2>Your notes stay exactly where they are.</h2><div class="port-columns"><ol class="port-steps"><li><h3>Extract the theme</h3><p>Download the ZIP and copy its <code>Santi020k</code> folder into <code>&lt;vault&gt;/.obsidian/themes/</code>. Use your custom configuration folder if you have changed it.</p></li><li><h3>Choose Santi020k</h3><p>In Settings → Appearance, select Santi020k under Themes. Choose Light, Dark, or Adapt to system as your base color scheme. Restart Obsidian if the theme does not appear.</p></li><li><h3>Bring it to your phone</h3><p>With Obsidian Sync, enable Themes and snippets under Vault configuration sync on both devices. After sync finishes, restart the mobile app and select Santi020k under Appearance. Other sync tools must include the configuration folder.</p></li></ol><div class="port-card"><h3>A simple, local theme</h3><p>No plugin is required. Your native fonts, text size, editing controls, and mobile keyboard behavior are preserved.</p><p>This is a manual installation. The theme is not yet listed in Obsidian’s community directory.</p><p>The theme folder must contain files named <code>theme.css</code> and <code>manifest.json</code>. The ZIP already uses those names.</p><Link href="https://help.obsidian.md/sync/settings" newTab>Obsidian Sync settings</Link></div></div></section>
  <section id="coverage" class="site-shell port-section"><Eyebrow>Considered in both appearances</Eyebrow><h2>From the first sentence to the next connection.</h2><div class="port-columns"><div><h3>Reading and writing</h3><p>Coordinated headings, links, selections, code blocks, tables, and quotations. Syntax stays readable on the canvas and selected text.</p><h3>The surrounding workspace</h3><p>Navigation, tabs, popovers, graph colors, focus borders, and status colors follow the same palette. Mobile keeps the app’s native layout.</p></div><div class="port-card"><h3>Update or restore</h3><p>Replace only the theme’s CSS and manifest to update. Select the default theme before removing the Santi020k folder to restore the original appearance. Your notes are untouched.</p><p>Other themes, CSS snippets, and plugins can override styling. Try a clean vault when checking a visual conflict.</p></div></div><div class="port-related"><Link href="/iphone/">Build a matching iPhone setup</Link><Link href="/neovim/">Continue in Neovim</Link></div></section>
</ProductLayout>
